From e1e9217de6c625f1b068b51bbb5f3658ca29328b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:08:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Tower icons: elevation drawings of the ten tallest towers
 on the map

A small, minimalist elevation of each tower stands on its pin once the map
is zoomed in far enough that the pin is no longer clustered (zoom 12+).
The icons share one scale, so heights compare truthfully; MapLibre's
collision detection hides an icon that would overlap a taller tower's
icon. Clicking an icon opens the tower's panel. The drawings are made by
scripts/tower-icons/gen.py into public/tower-icons/ (SVG + index.json),
so more towers can be added a batch at a time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SzHLihdfzaJUPJ2HoM9jcu
